        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"lagerlof-gosta-berlings-saga-baef76cd44bc6283\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.96,\"analysis\":\"Marianne’s sentence presents as true an enduring, exclusive state of love: she has never been able to love anyone except Gösta. It is therefore strongly truth-conditional even though she is consciously trying to win him back and may not yet fully experience the feeling she avows. The highlighted sentence makes no substantial commitment or undertaking, and its calculated performance supplies no independent expressive/reflexive force.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The later narration says Marianne’s love had not been dead but that she became conscious of it only after Gösta left. This complicates the avowal’s sincerity and self-knowledge, but not its strongly truth-conditional mode.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Marianne directly addresses Gösta with the spoken avowal, “jag har aldrig kunnat älska någon annan än dig” (“I have never been able to love anyone but you”).\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Marianne utters the avowal while trying to prevent Gösta from leaving. The narrator explicitly frames her conduct as an attempt to play the passionate lover because she does not want to lose him, and Gösta calls her words a lie. Immediately after his departure, however, she experiences overwhelming longing and recognizes that her love had been obscured rather than dead. Thus the utterance is strategically delivered and impaired by incomplete self-knowledge, while possibly being retrospectively true; those complications concern sincerity and context rather than its core T force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Gösta, jag har aldrig kunnat älska någon annan än dig.”\",\"supports\":\"The declarative sentence explicitly presents Marianne’s exclusive and enduring love for Gösta as true, strongly supporting T.\",\"confidence\":1.0},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Själviakttagelsen satt och hånlog åt hennes försök att spela förälskad” and “hon försökte spela passionerad.”\",\"supports\":\"The narration characterizes her delivery as a self-conscious attempt to act loving and passionate, undermining any inference from intensity to expressive/reflexive E.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Gösta responds: “Du talar inte sanning ... jag ser, att du ljuger.”\",\"supports\":\"The addressee construes the utterance as a truth claim and rejects it as false; this reinforces its T mode while raising contextual doubt about sincerity.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"After Gösta leaves, the narration says love emerges in Marianne’s heart and explains: “Hennes kärlek hade ju inte varit död,” but she had been unable to feel its power after her illness.\",\"supports\":\"The subsequent narration complicates the charge of lying by suggesting dormant love and delayed self-recognition, without changing the original utterance’s assertive force.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is tagged as an affirmative, perfect-tense, exclusive-target form and reviewed as a valid explicit I–you love expression.\",\"supports\":\"The supplied linguistic metadata corroborates the reading of the highlighted clause as an explicit exclusive love avowal.\",\"confidence\":0.99}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core avowal. The strategic performance, disputed sincerity, and later awakening of feeling are contextual complications adequately described without P, E, or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
